## Summary

**Windows users experience zombie processes accumulating in Task Manager after closing Auto-Claude.** Each time the app is closed and reopened, additional orphaned processes remain running, eventually causing system resource issues and blocking reinstallation.

This issue was previously identified and a fix was proposed in PR #753, but **the PR was closed without being merged** due to a mistaken belief that the issue was already fixed. Our comprehensive investigation confirms the fix was never applied.

---

## Related Issues & PRs

| Type | Number | Title | Status | Relationship |
|------|--------|-------|--------|--------------|
| Issue | #641 | Auto-Claude closing doesn't kill process | OPEN | **Root issue** - identical symptoms |
| Issue | #607 | Installer fails with "close application" error | OPEN | **Symptom** - zombie processes block installer |
| Issue | #762 | Claude Agent SDK leaves orphaned processes | OPEN | Related (different root cause - SDK bug) |
| PR | #753 | fix(windows): kill process tree on app close | **CLOSED** | **Fix was never merged!** |

---

## Why PR #753 Was Never Merged

PR #753 by @Orinks proposed the correct fix using `taskkill /T /F /PID` on Windows. However, the author closed it with the comment:

> "I think this has already been fixed on develop branch."

**This was incorrect.** Our investigation confirms:
- No `process-utils.ts` utility was ever created
- No `taskkill` is used in the agent process management code
- `agent-process.ts` still uses `SIGTERM`/`SIGKILL` which don't work on Windows
- The PTY daemon is never killed on shutdown

---

## Root Cause Analysis

We ran a comprehensive 12-agent parallel investigation that identified **5 verified root causes**:

### 1. SIGTERM/SIGKILL Don't Work on Windows (CRITICAL)

**File:** `apps/frontend/src/main/agent/agent-process.ts` (lines 700, 705)

```typescript
killProcess(taskId: string): boolean {
  // ...
  agentProcess.process.kill('SIGTERM');  // Ignored on Windows

  setTimeout(() => {
    if (!agentProcess.process.killed) {
      agentProcess.process.kill('SIGKILL');  // Ignored on Windows
    }
  }, 5000);
  // ...
}
```

**Problem:** Windows doesn't support POSIX signals. `SIGTERM` and `SIGKILL` are either ignored or don't propagate to child processes. Python agent processes and their children survive.

### 2. No Process Tree Killing (CRITICAL)

**Missing:** `taskkill /T /F /PID` or `tree-kill` package

Windows requires explicit tree killing to terminate child processes. The current code only attempts to kill the parent process, leaving all children orphaned:

```
Electron Main Process
  └── Python interpreter (killed)
      └── Claude Agent SDK (ORPHANED - stays running)
          └── git.exe, bash.exe, etc. (ORPHANED - stays running)
```

### 3. PTY Daemon Never Killed (CRITICAL)

**File:** `apps/frontend/src/main/terminal/pty-daemon-client.ts` (lines 131-138, 403-409)

The PTY daemon is spawned with `detached: true` and `unref()`, but the `shutdown()` method only disconnects the socket - it never kills the daemon process:

```typescript
// Line 131-138: Daemon spawned as detached
this.daemonProcess = spawn(process.execPath, [daemonPath], {
  detached: true,
  stdio: 'ignore',
});
this.daemonProcess.unref();

// Line 403-409: shutdown() only disconnects, never kills!
shutdown(): void {
  this.isShuttingDown = true;
  this.disconnect();  // Only closes socket
  // Missing: this.daemonProcess.kill()
}
```

### 4. killAllProcesses() Doesn't Wait (HIGH)

**File:** `apps/frontend/src/main/agent/agent-process.ts` (lines 721-729)

```typescript
async killAllProcesses(): Promise<void> {
  const killPromises = this.state.getRunningTaskIds().map((taskId) => {
    return new Promise<void>((resolve) => {
      this.killProcess(taskId);
      resolve();  // Resolves immediately without waiting!
    });
  });
  await Promise.all(killPromises);  // All resolve instantly
}
```

### 5. App-Updater Interval Never Cleared (MEDIUM)

**File:** `apps/frontend/src/main/app-updater.ts` (lines 192-200)

A `setInterval` runs every 4 hours but is never cleared on shutdown, keeping the Node event loop alive.

---

## Process Accumulation Flow

```
User starts Auto-Claude
    ↓
PTY daemon spawned (detached: true, unref())
Agent processes spawned (Python → Claude SDK → git, bash, etc.)
    ↓
User closes Auto-Claude (clicks X)
    ↓
before-quit fires
  ├─ agentManager.killAll() → Uses SIGTERM/SIGKILL (IGNORED ON WINDOWS)
  ├─ terminalManager.killAll() → Doesn't wait for Windows PTY exit
  ├─ PTY daemon → NEVER KILLED (shutdown() only disconnects socket)
  └─ App-updater interval → NEVER CLEARED
    ↓
App exits IMMEDIATELY (async cleanup not awaited)
    ↓
ORPHANED PROCESSES REMAIN:
  • PTY daemon process (node.exe)
  • Python agent processes (python.exe)
  • Child processes (cmd.exe, pwsh.exe, git.exe, etc.)
    ↓
User restarts Auto-Claude
    ↓
NEW processes spawned + OLD processes still running
    ↓
ACCUMULATION: 2x, 3x, 4x... processes in Task Manager
```

---

## The Correct Pattern Already Exists!

**File:** `apps/frontend/src/main/ipc-handlers/task/worktree-handlers.ts` (lines 3033-3061)

This file already implements the correct Windows pattern:

```typescript
if (process.platform === 'win32') {
  try {
    createPRProcess.kill();
    if (createPRProcess.pid) {
      setTimeout(() => {
        try {
          spawn('taskkill', ['/pid', createPRProcess.pid!.toString(), '/f', '/t'], {
            stdio: 'ignore',
            detached: true
          }).unref();
        } catch {
          // Process may already be dead
        }
      }, 5000);
    }
  } catch {
    // Process may already be dead
  }
} else {
  createPRProcess.kill('SIGTERM');
  setTimeout(() => {
    try {
      createPRProcess.kill('SIGKILL');
    } catch {
      // Process may already be dead
    }
  }, 5000);
}
```

**This pattern needs to be applied to `agent-process.ts`.**

---

## Proposed Solution

### Option A: Use `tree-kill` Package (Recommended)

```bash
npm install tree-kill
npm install -D @types/tree-kill
```

Create `apps/frontend/src/main/utils/process-utils.ts`:

```typescript
import treeKill from 'tree-kill';
import { spawn } from 'child_process';

export function killProcessTree(pid: number): Promise<void> {
  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
    treeKill(pid, 'SIGKILL', (err) => {
      if (err) reject(err);
      else resolve();
    });
  });
}
```

### Option B: Direct `taskkill` (No New Dependency)

Use the pattern from `worktree-handlers.ts` directly in `agent-process.ts`.

### Files to Modify

1. **`apps/frontend/src/main/agent/agent-process.ts`**
   - Update `killProcess()` to use `taskkill /T /F /PID` on Windows
   - Make `killAllProcesses()` actually await process termination

2. **`apps/frontend/src/main/terminal/pty-daemon-client.ts`**
   - Update `shutdown()` to kill the daemon process before disconnecting

3. **`apps/frontend/src/main/index.ts`**
   - Ensure `before-quit` handler awaits all cleanup operations

4. **`apps/frontend/src/main/app-updater.ts`**
   - Store interval ID and clear on shutdown

---

## How to Verify the Fix

1. Start Auto-Claude on Windows
2. Open a terminal and/or start a build task
3. Close the app
4. Open Task Manager → Details tab
5. Search for: `node.exe`, `python.exe`, `cmd.exe`, `pwsh.exe`
6. **Expected:** No orphaned processes with Auto-Claude as parent
7. Repeat 3-5 times to verify no accumulation

---

## Environment

- **OS:** Windows 10/11
- **Affected versions:** All versions (issue has existed since PTY daemon was introduced)
- **Severity:** High - causes resource leaks, blocks reinstallation, degrades system performance

