## Bug #1: `reactiveTokenRefresh()` Does Not Propagate `errorCode` (CRITICAL)

### Location
`apps/frontend/src/main/claude-profile/token-refresh.ts` lines 495-501

### Evidence

When `reactiveTokenRefresh()` fails, it does NOT include the `errorCode` field in the return value:

```typescript
// Lines 495-501 in reactiveTokenRefresh()
if (!refreshResult.success || !refreshResult.accessToken || !refreshResult.refreshToken || !refreshResult.expiresAt) {
  return {
    token: null,
    wasRefreshed: false,
    error: `Reactive refresh failed: ${refreshResult.error}`
    // ❌ MISSING: errorCode: refreshResult.errorCode
  };
}
```

**Compare to `ensureValidToken()` which correctly includes it:**

```typescript
// Lines 393-397 in ensureValidToken()
return {
  token: creds.token,
  wasRefreshed: false,
  error: `Token refresh failed: ${refreshResult.error}`,
  errorCode: refreshResult.errorCode  // ✅ CORRECTLY INCLUDED
};
```

### Impact

In `usage-monitor.ts` line 1139, `handleAuthFailure()` attempts to detect permanent token revocation:

```typescript
// Line 1139 in handleAuthFailure()
if (refreshResult.errorCode === 'invalid_grant') {
  this.debugLog('[UsageMonitor] Profile needs re-authentication (invalid refresh token): ' + profileId);
  this.needsReauthProfiles.add(profileId);
}
```

**This check will NEVER succeed** because `reactiveTokenRefresh()` never returns `errorCode`. The profile is never marked as needing re-authentication, so the system keeps retrying with the revoked token.

### Fix Required

```typescript
// In reactiveTokenRefresh() lines 495-501, add errorCode:
return {
  token: null,
  wasRefreshed: false,
  error: `Reactive refresh failed: ${refreshResult.error}`,
  errorCode: refreshResult.errorCode  // ADD THIS LINE
};
```

