## Bug 4: Unhandled Promise Rejection in IPC Handler (HIGH)

### Problem

The `CHANGELOG_GENERATE` handler is async but uses `ipcMain.on()` instead of `ipcMain.handle()`. Unhandled rejections are silently ignored.

### Evidence

`apps/frontend/src/main/ipc-handlers/changelog-handlers.ts:104-131`

```typescript
ipcMain.on(
  IPC_CHANNELS.CHANGELOG_GENERATE,
  async (_, request: ChangelogGenerationRequest) => {  // ← async with .on()
    // ...
    specs = await changelogService.loadTaskSpecs(...);  // ← If this throws, error is lost
    changelogService.generateChangelog(...);
  }
);
```

With `ipcMain.on()`, if the async callback throws, the error is not propagated to the renderer. The user sees no feedback.

### Suggested Fix

Either use `ipcMain.handle()` or wrap in try/catch:

```typescript
ipcMain.on(
  IPC_CHANNELS.CHANGELOG_GENERATE,
  async (_, request: ChangelogGenerationRequest) => {
    try {
      // ... existing logic
    } catch (error) {
      changelogService.emitError(request.projectId, `Failed to start generation: ${error.message}`);
    }
  }
);
```

