## Bug 5: Event Listener Memory Leak (MEDIUM)

### Problem

Event listeners on `changelogService` are registered but never unregistered.

### Evidence

`apps/frontend/src/main/ipc-handlers/changelog-handlers.ts:34-60`

```typescript
export function registerChangelogHandlers(): void {
  // These listeners are NEVER removed
  changelogService.on('generation-progress', (projectId, progress) => { ... });
  changelogService.on('generation-complete', (projectId, result) => { ... });
  changelogService.on('generation-error', (projectId, error) => { ... });
  changelogService.on('rate-limit', (projectId, rateLimitInfo) => { ... });
}
```

If `registerChangelogHandlers()` is called multiple times (HMR, app restart), listeners accumulate.

### Suggested Fix

Track and remove listeners:

```typescript
let cleanupFunctions: (() => void)[] = [];

export function registerChangelogHandlers(): void {
  // Clean up previous listeners
  cleanupFunctions.forEach(cleanup => cleanup());
  cleanupFunctions = [];

  const progressHandler = (projectId, progress) => { ... };
  changelogService.on('generation-progress', progressHandler);
  cleanupFunctions.push(() => changelogService.off('generation-progress', progressHandler));

  // ... same for other listeners
}
```

