## Proposed Fix

### 1. Add Project Context to Listeners

Modify `setupInsightsListeners()` to accept `projectId` and validate incoming events:

```typescript
export function setupInsightsListeners(activeProjectId: string): () => void {
  const store = useInsightsStore.getState;

  const unsubStreamChunk = window.electronAPI.onInsightsStreamChunk(
    (projectId, chunk: InsightsStreamChunk) => {
      // Only process events for the active project
      if (projectId !== activeProjectId) return;

      switch (chunk.type) {
        case 'text':
          store().appendStreamingContent(chunk.content);
          // ...
      }
    }
  );

  // Apply same pattern to all other listeners
  // ...
}
```

### 2. Update Component to Pass ProjectId

```typescript
// In Insights.tsx
useEffect(() => {
  loadInsightsSession(projectId);
  const cleanup = setupInsightsListeners(projectId);  // Pass projectId
  return cleanup;
}, [projectId]);
```

### 3. Clear Streaming State on Project Switch

```typescript
export async function loadInsightsSession(projectId: string): Promise<void> {
  // Clear streaming state before loading new session
  const state = useInsightsStore.getState();
  state.clearStreamingContent();
  state.clearToolsUsed();
  state.setCurrentTool(null);
  state.setStatus({ phase: 'idle', message: '' });

  const result = await window.electronAPI.getInsightsSession(projectId);
  // ...
}
```

### 4. Fix Empty ProjectId Fallbacks

Pass `projectId` to `addMessage` and `finalizeStreamingMessage` actions, or store `activeProjectId` in the Zustand state.

